                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "baca60d9-fd83-3b62-ab16-cde4b7bc5b87",
                "word": "Huggie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d9810c10-89c2-4b19-a4c3-2b013236f4f7",
                        "entry_id": "baca60d9-fd83-3b62-ab16-cde4b7bc5b87",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Huggies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e299f6e3-6e40-3496-8eeb-25dcf42ba475",
                        "entry_id": "baca60d9-fd83-3b62-ab16-cde4b7bc5b87",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A diaper made by the Huggies company."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal",
                            "uncommon"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b17ba3f8-2656-4e97-a187-7dcf178a3f9d",
                                "sense_id": "e299f6e3-6e40-3496-8eeb-25dcf42ba475",
                                "text": "\"Does anyone have a Huggie?\"\nIf this disposable diaper trend continues, it's also possible that CO's in wartime will no longer be conscientious objectors, but rather cloth objectors."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb15088e-2a96-4eb8-aa39-f57d5155e775",
                                "sense_id": "e299f6e3-6e40-3496-8eeb-25dcf42ba475",
                                "text": "I was on a long road trip with my 3-year-old daughter and newborn twin boys. It was about 2:00 in the morning. […] All of a sudden I realized I had to pee. Badly. There was no way I was pulling into a rest stop at this hour all by myself. […] After a few frantic minutes, I had a brilliant plan. I reached into the twins' diaper bag, pulled out a diaper and thought, \"Yes!\" slid my pants down, placed not one, but two Huggies® under myself, and aahhhh...sweet relief."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fc88276-1cea-4482-8585-ae108ca3f8f8",
                                "sense_id": "e299f6e3-6e40-3496-8eeb-25dcf42ba475",
                                "text": "Zac rubbed his red eyes. \"She's done a poo.\"\n\"It's all right, I'll go,\" said Merridy, relieved to have an excuse. She put her sun hat back on and went to fetch a Huggie from the supply that she kept handy in the spare bedroom."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "503c7610-442c-49e8-a5b9-bb036d9a53a1",
                                "sense_id": "e299f6e3-6e40-3496-8eeb-25dcf42ba475",
                                "text": "There have been some excellent recent examples of firms extending the life of a customer by adapting a marketing strategy. Kimberly-Clark, manufacturer of Huggies disposable nappies, was subject to the limitations imposed by the fact that the 'life' of a Huggie customer (the baby) averaged only 18 months, until the child became toilet-trained. Market research also revealed a considerable degree of guilt among parents."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
